Module skeel "Fair Weather" {
  Description "Links outward from the Reach: a light seen at sea after a ship was left in the Slack, a stranger's rubbing of the Prefect's table, and the almanack woman who walks from here to the Bowl.".

  // ── A world event, read: the Holm Lantern's night log ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // If, in the world, the ship Remainder was left in the Slack (the Grand Tour's), a lamp-keeper who has kept the log
  // of an empty sea for years is the first to put it down. Said once, for the room.
  Observe lore_log_light at lamp_room when befell(remainder_kept) "Under the night log of the Lantern, in Loveday Kitto's round hand, a line that is not about weather: LIGHT AT THE EDGE OF THE SEA, 2 A.M., NO SHIP. IT WAS STILL. It is entered again the next night, and the next, always at the same hour, with the same three words after it, and the third night a small mark in the margin, like a tally, that is not Loveday's.".
  Observe lore_taproom_south at taproom when befell(slack_opened) "In the corner by the settle two drovers are explaining to a pilot who has not asked that a great house in a town on the south coast has a black square let into its floor. The pilot is looking at his beer. 'A hole in a floor,' he says. 'We have the sea for that.' Mother Jago, polishing a pot, says that if the sea ever lets a house keep a stair she would like to be told.".

  // ── A visitor from elsewhere: the Prefect's table ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Discovery lore_table_same "Loveday has seen the rubbing of the Prefect's table and says the foot-rule on it is the same as the one on the lamp-room wall.".
  Topic lore_loveday_table with loveday "Show Loveday Kitto the rubbing of the Prefect's table" when holding(actor, pharos_rubbing) once {
    Says "Loveday lays it on the lamp-room floor and weights the corners with the tin of wicks, the matches, and two boots. She reads it with her whole arm, the way she reads the sea. 'Columns of numbers,' she says, 'and beside them a column that was scrubbed and never came clean. I know a scrubbed column. Look.' She turns the lamp-stand a quarter so that the light slants, and on the iron foot, beside the fish and the flame, under fifty years of polish, there is a mark you could take for a maker's. She sets her thumb over it, and then she measures the rubbing's foot-rule against the one painted on the wall, twice, and it is the same length. She rolls the rubbing carefully and does not hand it back at once.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_table_same). }
  }

  // ── The almanack woman ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Jessamy Cattermole walks a loop that no map draws: the Reach, the Bowl of Ammerlin, Merrowdale, the Lim valley,
  // the Wray, and back to the sea. She sells almanacks, each printed in a different town, each for a different year.
  Discovery lore_cattermole_skeel "Jessamy Cattermole, who sells almanacks, was at the Admiral at Michaelmas and has gone up the coast road to the Bowl of Ammerlin, where a man named Halm pays by the inch for anything with a mark on it that is not writing. Parson Hosken gave her a stub of wax.".
  Topic lore_jago_cattermole with jago "Ask Mother Jago who else has come down the coast road this autumn" when true once {
    Says "'Cattermole,' says Jago at once, as if the name were a plate she had been waiting to put down. 'The almanack woman. Six towns' worth in a leather satchel, and no two of them agree what year it is. She says it does not matter, they all keep Michaelmas on the same night.' She wipes her hands. 'Sold the Reeve a calendar he did not want and Parson Hosken a stub of rubbing-wax he did. Went off up the north road to a place called Ammerlin, to a man called Halm who pays by the inch for marks that are not writing. If you see her, she owes me for four pints and a stable.'".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_cattermole_skeel). }
  }

  // ── An entry point: a letter for the Tolleth packet ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Mother Jago's man cooks aboard a packet out of Tolleth, the Dorothea, and writes once a year. She has a letter and
  // nobody to carry it south. The Dorothea sails on the noon ebb from the quay at Tolleth; Captain Bascom will know him.
  Item lore_jago_letter "Mother Jago's letter, folded in a sketch of the Admiral" is map at limbo owned by jago.
  Relation lore_jagoLetter(group).
  Topic lore_jago_packet with jago "Ask Mother Jago whether she has word for anyone on the Tolleth packet" when true once {
    Says "'Now who told you?' says Jago, and puts down the pot. 'My man is cook on the Dorothea, Tolleth packet, Captain Bascom, salt south and lamp-oil to the rock at Skerrow and back. He writes at Michaelmas and I write at Lady Day and it has not once crossed.' She digs under the counter and brings up a letter folded inside a drawing of the Admiral, the roof, the sign, a cat. 'If you are going that way. The board on the quay at Tolleth gives her sailings in chalk. Tell Bascom it is for her cook, and tell him the cat is well. Do not tell him the roof.'".
    On discuss { Give lore_jago_letter to actor. Assert lore_jagoLetter(actor). }
  }

  // ── Three papers and a face from elsewhere, each shown to someone who would know what to do with it ───────────────
  Discovery lore_mask_notch "Parson Hosken, shown a grey mask with a single notch for a brow, says the notch is a count of one, and that he has preached over the Holm's cell for twenty years without once asking what it kept.".
  Topic lore_hosken_mask with hosken "Show Parson Hosken the grey mask with the notch" when holding(actor, keeper_mask) once {
    Says "Hosken holds it by the rim, as he holds the chalice, and turns it to the window. 'No eyes,' he says. 'No mouth. A face made to be looked at and not to look.' His thumb finds the notch. 'One,' he says. 'Not a sin, not a saint's day. One. As on the bench in the cell, where the strokes come in rows and the rows end.' 'Somebody was meant to keep this count and stand where it could see the sea.' He sets the mask on the pew very gently, face up, and does not take his hand away from it for some time.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_mask_notch). }
  }
  Discovery lore_letter_lead "Bartle Tonkin, shown a letter from the Collegium of Lesser Instruments, says the Collegium wants things that work and that the only working thing on the ropewalk is his one lead-line, which he casts once a year and writes down.".
  Topic lore_bartle_letter with bartle "Show Bartle Tonkin the letter of the Collegium of Lesser Instruments" when holding(actor, collegium_letter) once {
    Says "Bartle reads it with his lips, and then reads the seal. 'Friend of working things,' he says. 'There is a college that thinks well of a hank of tarred cord. I never knew.' He wipes his hands on his apron for longer than they need. 'I have a lead-line. One. I take it out over the bar every Michaelmas, a cast to the foot, and put the numbers in a book that nobody has asked for in thirty years.' He looks at the letter, and at the book on its nail, and takes the book down and wipes its cover with his sleeve before he puts it back.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_letter_lead). }
  }
  Discovery lore_surety_jago "Mother Jago, shown the Ninth Valuer's note on a surety, says she stood surety once for a boat's caulking and that nobody wrote down which keeping she was standing for.".
  Topic lore_jago_surety with jago "Show Mother Jago the Ninth Valuer's note on a surety" when holding(actor, surety_terms) once {
    Says "Jago reads the strip at arm's length and then holds it to the lamp. 'Answers for the keeping named,' she says, 'and where none is named, for all.' She puts a thumb on the last words. 'I put my name to the Patience's new planking, the spring Skeel was short. Nobody wrote what I was standing for. I thought I was standing for a plank.' She hands it back, and goes to see to a pot that does not need seeing to, and for a while the taproom hears her thinking about the whole ship.".
    On discuss { Assert knows(actor, lore_surety_jago). }
  }

  // ── The Scarth light, down the coast ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  // Lamp-keepers read each other's lights. Loveday Kitto has never seen the Scarth rock, but she knows its character
  // from eleven miles of sea, and puts down what she sees of it in the same hand as the weather.
  Observe lore_log_scarth_kept at lamp_room when befell(scarth_kept) and not befell(scarth_lost) "Under the night log, in Loveday Kitto's round hand, a line that is not about weather: THE SCARTH LIGHT WAS LIT AT DUSK AND STOOD ALL NIGHT AND WAS LIT AT DAWN. She has underlined ALL NIGHT. 'You'd think that the rule,' she says, 'not the news. But I have been keeping a light thirty years and I have seen it go out on a rock with a keeper in it. I put it down when one doesn't.'".
  Observe lore_log_scarth_lost at lamp_room when befell(scarth_lost) "Under the night log, in Loveday Kitto's round hand, a line that is not about weather: THE SCARTH LIGHT WAS LIT, AND THE KEEPER'S WINDOW WAS NOT. She has not underlined it. She has turned the log a quarter on the table, as one turns a slate, so that the next page is the one that faces her. 'It is a long way to be sorry from,' she says, 'but I find I am.'".
}
